1.05

  Summary: additive patch, idle PDA reworked, companion and patrol freeze fixed, wounded stand-up, poses restored, relaxed idle pose option, MCM config

  First release of this fork of Chemzs's xAGNA. Every entry below is a change against that original.

  Compatibility
    - The script layer was rewritten. The data, the animation and state tables, now sits apart from the
      code, and the code adds its changes at load, wrapping or replacing a vanilla function only where
      that fits. The original instead shipped whole copies of the game's core animation and state
      scripts, which overwrote the shared state machine. Any mod that also touched it lost, and
      companions and patrols could freeze. The additive rewrite should clear several of the reported
      bugs and odd behavior. The OMFs ship as assets, as before.
    - With the latest demonized exes, a Behavior option sets the relaxed standing idle pose, from the
      vanilla player pose to one varied per NPC. Older builds ignore it and keep the vanilla pose.

  Changes
    - Idle PDA reworked.
      The original drew it on the shared idle. Every NPC pulled one out, and the multi-step draw froze them in place.
      That blocked patrol and companions. The idle is instant again.
      Now only standing, calm, out-of-combat NPCs near you occasionally take one out. Never companions, dropped the moment danger appears.
    - Wounded NPCs play a stand-up animation as they recover, instead of snapping upright.
    - The greeting and PDA an NPC plays when you walk up to a commander no longer fire on every approach.
      Each rolls its own chance, so most approaches are a plain greeting.

  Animations restored
    - Sentry, listening and searching NPCs play their poses on every weapon slot again.
    - NPCs searching for a bloodsucker play the alert pose again.
    - The unarmed idle cycles its 4 variants again.
    - Heavy-wounded variant 3 keeps its own distinct pose again.
    - Standing smoke plays the smoking animation again.

  Animations kept
    - The free-hand punch, the commander, guard and talk poses, the standing medical and wounded postures, and the re-animated motion set are unchanged.

  MCM
    - Added a Behavior page: chances for the greeting, the PDA on approach, a commander's PDA, and an
      idle NPC's PDA, plus a wounded stand-up toggle and the relaxed idle pose choice. A chance slider at 0 turns it off.
    - Added a Log level control and an immediate-flush toggle for live tracing.
    - Added an Animation sampling toggle that records the states NPCs actually play to xagna_animations.log, for confirming the mod's motions fire.

  Install
    - Delete the previous xAGNA before installing. It no longer ships the old override script files. Leaving them in place re-applies the old behavior.
